    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Sometimes the capital is given as fractions of one total.\n\nSuppose A invests 1/2 of the capital and B invests 1/3. The rest belongs to C.\n\nC = 1 − 1/2 − 1/3 = 1/6.\nSo A : B : C = 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/6 = 3 : 2 : 1.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Fractions look awkward only until you clear the denominators.\n\nMultiply every fraction by the same LCM. Here the LCM is 6:\n1/2, 1/3, 1/6 → 3, 2, 1.\n\nNow it is an ordinary partnership ratio.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_2": {
      "id": "q_2",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "A invests 2/5 of the total capital, B invests 1/4, and C invests the rest. What is A : B : C?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "input": {
        "type": "CHOICE",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "8 : 5 : 7"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "2 : 1 : 2"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "8 : 5 : 3"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "label": "5 : 4 : 11"
          }
        ]
      },
      "questionReference": {
        "mode": "INLINE",
